	order_index: 1
	filename: "stuck_in_the_burb"
	title: "[?] Stuck in the BURB"
	icon: "minestuck:scalemate_applescab"
	subtitle: ["MOD : Minestuck"]
	default_quest_shape: ""
	default_hide_dependency_lines: false
	quests: [
		{
			title: "Remnants of a Lost Game"
			x: -10.75d
			y: -5.75d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "MOD : Minestuck"
			description: [
				"&7Hey Bandit, keep an eye out while you are looking for Iron and Copper just above the Deepslate. If that old cold is left in, then you should find something... quite interesting."
				""
				"&7Right now, the bosses are helping you break out of the system, while myself and the other Researchers are helping you survive until then."
				""
				"&7But what you just found? Might be just the thing that will help ALL of us. Especially you."
				""
				"&7You may or may not have found some of this blue... material, out when searching for Chromatic Iron. It's called Cruxite, and it's where we'll start."
			]
			dependencies: ["45D2E30FD73E062E"]
			id: "2019F6F56C5A7D4B"
			tasks: [{
				id: "387B7D9AC801F060"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:raw_cruxite"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Lost in the System"
			x: -9.5d
			y: -5.75d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Okay, Bandit, the thing you found is called Cruxite. It's... hm, where should I begin."
				""
				"&7Well, long before the the FOP switched their FOPGame Server to this Vault Hunters, there used to be another game. Nobody knows who made it, but it was as expansive as the FOPGame Server. The game was known as SBurb. "
				""
				"&7Four or so years after SBurb came out, it suddenly went offline, and no further word or trace could be found of the original company. Exactly one week later, the FOPGame Server launched, with only a small shareholder report from the FOP mentioning that they had acquired the SBURB game servers. SBURB then faded from memory..."
				""
				"&7What was it though? Well, I need to do some research... but explore more in the same areas as Cruxite. See if you can find some Uranium Chunks for me... If you can, it'll confirm my suspicions."
				""
				"&7It'll be very hard to find naturally, but you might be able to use some Cruxite and a bunch of other Uranium Ore to \"glitch\" out a couple pieces?"
			]
			dependencies: ["2019F6F56C5A7D4B"]
			id: "48F1C97A76078762"
			tasks: [{
				id: "63EC3F17062D9873"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:raw_uranium"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "044DD37481499ADE"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Mysteriously Intact"
			x: -8.25d
			y: -5.75d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7I WAS right. Amazing!"
				""
				"&7Er, right then, what was SBurb? It was basically a huge sandbox game. But instead of being 'digitized' into the game, it was OVERLAYED on top of the real world. You could fight creatures, summon and build things, craft, join friends, etc. And eventually you could travel to other worlds, other places. Not like the Vaults you can run..."
				""
				"&7And all of these was done in reality, in your own house, neighborhood, etc. The things you earned and built in the game, had physical presence. And your finding things from that game here..."
				""
				"&7Notice how Cruxite items can't be Digitized? That's because the FOP fought hard to make people forget about SBURB. If they have chat filters watching for SBurb being mentioned....I know, let's call it uh... Minestuck instead!"
				""
				"&7For now, make yourself a Blank Disk. You'll need it soon..."
			]
			dependencies: ["48F1C97A76078762"]
			id: "1FCB0E4A2F267C82"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1062361A93D9D6A7"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:blank_disk"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "47189A6F496A3088"
				type: "choice"
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Frogs and Glitches"
			icon: "minestuck:cruxtruder"
			x: -4.5d
			y: -5.75d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "Glitch%"
			description: [
				"&7In the original version of Minestuck, you needed to find a \"Frog Temple\" to get access, which was just an 'in game' way of saying a store that sold Minestuck."
				""
				"&7But the funny thing was, if you already WERE playing Minestuck, certain stores were changed into ACTUAL 'Frog Temples'. But... we aren't likely to find a Frog Temple anymore, huh?"
				""
				"&7If we want to bring Minestuck back, we'll have to activate the code the old fashioned way : time to glitch things!"
				""
				"&7If you've followed the bosses' for a bit before jumping here, I think they gave you something called Unobtanium? "
				""
				"&7By crafting Unobtanium back and forth between Ingots and Blocks, you multiply them. This is a glitch, and one we'll use like a crowbar."
				""
				"&7Take that Blank Disk and combine it with Unobtanium to make a Cruxtruder."
			]
			dependencies: ["6A21DB08C3F1E5A7"]
			id: "52754C14A4625112"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5DAEFABBA7D83168"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:cruxtruder"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "01D871E744042061"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Stacked Queue"
			x: -5.75d
			y: -5.75d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Now, to add items to your Sylladex, select them in  your hotbar and hit V. The item will vanish and be put into an empty card in your Captchalogue Deck!"
				""
				"&7Try it with ONE cobblestone. You can usually Captchalogue up to a full stack, but not always. "
				""
				"&7Now, putting items into your Sylladex is easy. Taking them out is... a bit different. Starting out, your Sylladex starts in \"Stack\" mode. You can see what mode you are in by looking in the upper right of your Sylladex."
				""
				"&7In Stack mode, items are added to the left side of of the Sylladex. Each new item pushes the previous items to the right, \"stacking\" them onto each other."
				""
				"&7In \"Stack\" mode, you can only remove the left most item. If you Left Click the item, you pull it out of the Card and into your inventory. If you RIGHT Click, you remove the card WITH the item! Do that now, you'll need that soon."
			]
			dependencies: ["679B9480C543F403"]
			id: "6A21DB08C3F1E5A7"
			tasks: [{
				id: "65DEDDBC85A98C03"
				type: "item"
				title: "A Captchalogue Card with 1 Cobblestone"
				item: {
					id: "minestuck:captcha_card"
					Count: 1b
					tag: {
						punched: 0b
						contentID: "minecraft:cobblestone"
						contentSize: 1
					}
				}
				match_nbt: true
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "1D1B4EA005A717E9"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Round and Colorful"
			x: -5.75d
			y: -4.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Place out that Cruxtruder somewhere, you'll use it a bunch. It starts with a cover over the top of it, a white lid with a green symbol on it. Break this off with a pickaxe or something."
				""
				"&7The Cruxtruder is used to shape raw Cruxite into a more... useable form for Alchemy. You fill the Cruxtruder by Right Clicking Cruxite into the 'pipe'."
				""
				"&7Then you can Right Click the dark gray wheel on the side of the pipe to 'extrude' a Cruxite Dowel."
				""
				"&7Think of the Cruxite Dowel like an Iron Ingot. Except its the color you chose when you first woke up in the FOPGame Server. And I think this is the only place that color actually shows up.... huh."
			]
			dependencies: ["52754C14A4625112"]
			id: "0D54B906CCE3EE45"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2AF516E92DDFA74F"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:cruxite_dowel"
				weak_nbt_match: true
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "132308C580F62C39"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Punchy Alchemy"
			icon: "minestuck:punch_designix"
			x: -7.0d
			y: -4.5d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7The second machine you'll need is called the Punch Designix. Craft it and toss it down somewhere. "
				""
				"&7Remember that Captchalogue Card with the Cobblestone from earlier? Go grab it, as well as an empty Card. "
				""
				"&7The Punch Designix is used to 'punch' the data of an item onto a Captcha Card, for use in Alchemy."
				""
				"&7To do this, Right Click the empty Captchalogue Card onto the LEFT side of the machine, where there is a slot for the Card."
				""
				"&7Now take that Captcha Card with the Cobblestone and Right Click it onto the keyboard on the right side of the Designix. This will \"Punch\" the data of the cobblestone onto the blank Card."
				""
				"&7You can then Right Click and remove the first card. See how it has lines on it now? That means it's Punched and ready to use in Alchemy!"
			]
			dependencies: ["0D54B906CCE3EE45"]
			id: "79F57A93686BD76B"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7327ED690F64D76A"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:punch_designix"
				}
				{
					id: "51DBC4F101CAB58A"
					type: "item"
					title: "A PUNCHED Cobblestone Captchalogue Card"
					item: {
						id: "minestuck:captcha_card"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							punched: 1b
							contentID: "minecraft:cobblestone"
						}
					}
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "1244515E126514D8"
				type: "choice"
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Spinning Up"
			icon: "minestuck:totem_lathe"
			x: -8.25d
			y: -4.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7The third Alchemy machine is called the Totem Lathe. "
				""
				"&7This looks like a fairly complicated machine... and it kind of is! But also not. Don't worry, the basics are simple!"
				""
				"&7On one side is that green symbol you saw earlier. Down and right of that is a slot for a Captchalogue Card. Right Click that Punched Captcha Card from earlier to place it there."
				""
				"&7Next, just to the right of the green symbol is a square rod sticking out, with a checkerboard on one face. Right Click a Cruxite Dowel on the checkerboard to place it into the Lathe."
				""
				"&7Finally, at the top middle of the machine is a gray square with a lever on it. If everything is set up correctly, you can Right Click that square to cut the item data into that Dowel. With that, you can Right Click the shaped Dowel to remove it from the Lathe."
			]
			dependencies: ["79F57A93686BD76B"]
			id: "415FC4F6B22EA0F7"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "23D727C001C825BA"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:totem_lathe"
				}
				{
					id: "7846A48E511D3791"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "minestuck:cruxite_dowel"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							contentID: "minecraft:cobblestone"
						}
					}
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "6EF1761680E54AF8"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Finally Alchemy"
			x: -9.5d
			y: -4.5d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7The final machine, that pulls it all together, is the Alchemiter. It's a pretty big machine, but well worth the space I'd say."
				""
				"&7Using the Alchemiter is simple. To the side of the platform is a tall arm. Near the bottom of this arm is a platform, with a checkerboard much like the Totem Lathe had. Right Click the shaped Cruxite Dowel onto this platform."
				""
				"&7Now you can Right Click the Alchemiter platform itself to see what it costs to make the item carved into the Dowel, and set how many you want to make."
				""
				"&7To make items, you'll need to collect a resource called Grist, which comes in a variety of types. While you start with 20 Build Grist, the most common type... getting more might be a little more difficult..."
			]
			dependencies: ["415FC4F6B22EA0F7"]
			id: "10E2B9F70E803BDB"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7BC7BBD0B4D1BA52"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:alchemiter"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "10E83500EF2C7681"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Decked Out Inventory"
			x: -7.0d
			y: -5.75d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Okay Bandit, that Blank Disk is the first steps into Alchemy, or well, what SBurb... I mean Minestuck... calls Alchemy. It primarily involves using 4 machines and... well..."
				""
				"&7...Before you can understand Alchemy, I need to teach you about Minestuck's special inventory system called a Sylladex."
				""
				"&7To access your Sylladex, hit G. Don't worry about the other tabs here, for now we'll focus on the left-most one called your Captchalogue Deck. This is the heart of your Sylladex. Go ahead and click on the Sylladex button."
				""
				"&7Unless you somehow added Cards here, this should be empty, unfortunately. But we can easily fix that. Craft up some Captchalogue Cards, and put them in the slot next to the Sylladex button, then hit Use Item to add them to your Captchalogue Deck!"
			]
			dependencies: ["1FCB0E4A2F267C82"]
			id: "679B9480C543F403"
			tasks: [{
				id: "09894FCD2FC3A9D8"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:captcha_card"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "3DC3901F15850189"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Field Trip Cancelled"
			icon: "minestuck:client_disk"
			x: -5.75d
			y: -3.25d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "More like Well Done"
			description: [
				"&7Usually by now, Bandit, you would have connected to the full SBurb Server, and teleported yourself to the Medium: another world specially designed to your Color and Title you chose."
				""
				"&7Unfortunately, the Medium doesn't really exist in the FOPGame Server anymore. Well, no, it does...but it also doesn't. It's in a limbo state that isn't really useful to us, a lot of the FOPGame Server systems don't work correctly in it."
				""
				"&7I guess the 'power' of the SBurb and Minestuck system is messing with everything. Which is great...but also not great, because the Alchemy system needs a lot of items you could only find in the Medium..."
				""
				"&7Though, you probably already noticed the solution : the Shop Tablet has a section specifically for SBurb items we can 'fix', though they'll cost Tokens, which you may have already started to find."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["55A4B37D7392342A"]
			id: "0029F0BC75976423"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7491809FAFDDE7AB"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "The Gates"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Advanced Alchemy"
			x: -9.5d
			y: -3.25d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Alright, you know the basics of alchemy : Captchalogue an item, Punch it onto a card in the Designix, Carve that on a Dowel in the Totem Lathe, then use Grist at the Alchemizer to create it."
				""
				"&7But also, there are two ways of COMBINING Unpunched and (Punched) Cards into brand new items : With the Designix, or with the Totem Lathe."
				""
				"&7Example, a Rock Cookie. You can take a (Punched) Cobblestone card and a (Punched) Cookie card, and put both of them into the Totem Lathe. This will make a Rock Cookie shaped Cruxite Dowel. This is known as \\&\\&\\ (and) Alchemy."
				""
				"&7Another Example : Flowery Mossy Cobblestone. If you place a (Punched) Mossy Cobblestone card into the Designix (instead of a blank card!), and Right Click an UNPUNCHED Captchalogue Card with a Flower in it onto the keyboard, it'll punch the design onto the Mossy Cobblestone card. This is called || (or) alchemy."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["0029F0BC75976423"]
			id: "4EAEC7D5C5DD1893"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7EC8A51A321E0B04"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:rock_cookie"
				}
				{
					id: "38F8B3143405CE9D"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:flowery_mossy_cobblestone"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "2CD0CBCFFF3367EF"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Solid Note"
			x: 4.25d
			y: 0.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7If a Book and Quill aren't 'solid' enough for you to write messages to other assistants, you could always Alchemy up a Stone Tablet and a Carving Tool!"
				""
				"&7Put the Carving Tool in your offhand, and Right Click while holding the Stone Tablet. Now you can write, I mean carve, a message!"
				""
				"&7You can place the written slab down by Sneak + Right Clicking, but I'm not sure how that'll react with the FOPGame Servers now."
			]
			dependencies: ["4EAEC7D5C5DD1893"]
			id: "47B542CF3816510F"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "3105B5E43AB4CB6F"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:stone_tablet"
				}
				{
					id: "50A58A976333A73E"
