				table_id: 5632731352558517809L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "The Grist of the Matter"
			x: -7.678571428571416d
			y: -3.3035714285714377d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7So, originally in Minestuck your main way of obtaining Grist was by fighting creatures called Imps and Glicops. They'd match a type of Grist, and killing them would get you that Grist. "
				""
				"&7Not really an option in the current FOPGame Server I think... but there was another way to get Grist, and I think I just found the remnants of the code for it... Now is it still functional...."
				""
				"&7...mostly. Just change a few things before I'm locked out again, and..."
				""
				"&7Alright Bandit, I present to you the GristWidget 12000! Create this, slap it down, and then you can put any  Captcha Card containing an Alchemizable item in it, and with the press of a button..."
				""
				"&7...boom, you break the item back down into Grist! Well, a portion of the Grist. You'll get about 25% the cost of making the item. Best I could do while I still had access to that old code."
			]
			dependencies: ["10E2B9F70E803BDB"]
			size: 1.25d
			id: "55A4B37D7392342A"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1B94CAF87A772205"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:grist_widget"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "4540056C6470E594"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Nuclear Cooking"
			x: -4.5d
			y: -4.5d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Want to put that Raw Uranium to use? Why not make a Cookalyzer?"
				""
				"&7The Cookalyzer is an odd Minestuck Machine that is sort of like an upgraded Furnace... but not at the same time? But instead of Coal or Wood as it's fuel, it uses... Raw Uranium."
				""
				"&7Unlike a Furnace, it stores the fuel and only uses it when processing an item. One Raw Uranium can smelt HALF A STACK worth of items!"
				""
				"&7The downside, though? It can only smelt some items. Not Ores it seems, but making Charcoal, cooking food, etc is super fast. You have to click GO to smelt an item... for every item. That's another downside."
				""
				"&7Also, apparently due to the radiation of cooking, some items may not... turn out the same as they would in a Furnace. Just a warning!"
			]
			dependencies: ["0029F0BC75976423"]
			id: "4F927767F75DB147"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4018EF74C0948014"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:uranium_cooker"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "3187298F7FD11672"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "An Idea Too Good..."
			x: 4.25d
			y: 1.75d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7I've heard tales from when SBURB was online that you could make Golden Seeds that grew Gold."
				""
				"&7I mean, that's nothing really new to us. The last world you were trapped in, you had such seeds. Not here though..."
				""
				"&7Though I'd take all this with a grain of salt. It feels like... a bit of a troll."
			]
