		{
			title: "Esoteric Programming"
			x: 3.0d
			y: -3.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7~ATH is a... strange coding language from the original SBURB. Strange as it relied on things dieing to execute major code. "
				""
				"&7An ~ATF program is required to have a repeating bit of code, a loop, that never stops until the object it is bound to dies. Anything with a short life span is not valid, it seems. When the object dies, the rest of the program runs."
				""
				"&7It doesn't seem to have survived into Minestuck, other than a few references and that very heavy handbook you have there."
			]
			dependencies: ["5D1BFAD59386BF52"]
			id: "258105C3D1BEAC95"
			tasks: [{
				id: "51AFFBC78DCD23BE"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:tilldeath_handbook"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "12CDEC090F058A42"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Of Pens and Papers"
			x: 0.5d
			y: -3.25d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Back when SBURB was around, there were a lot of fan projects, big and small. Craft projects, fan stories, and even a whole pen and paper RPG based around SBURB. "
				""
				"&7This was called Tablestuck. It was made for big groups that regularly had small group sessions, and later would meet up for bigger adventures."
				""
				"&7This manual was added to SBURB as sort of an easter egg reward for all the work done on it."
			]
			dependencies: ["5D1BFAD59386BF52"]
			id: "6B425904D1CD374E"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1EF722445743492D"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:tablestuck_manual"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "363366AA6263D9CC"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Batty RP"
			x: 4.25d
			y: -3.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7FLARP was an in-game sort of minigame in the original SBURB, which would use 'bats' to create a play area, show player stats, and overall help run the game 'code' for FLARP participants."
				""
				"&7It doesn't seem that this has transferred into Minestuck, other than this handy but useless book."
